A loop over a const iterable is unrolled for a target with no host language.
This package loops over a two-element const list, so the unrolling is the two
iterations and nothing else: the else body belongs to the empty case and must
not be emitted beside them.

The empty case is the one that regressed -- the expansion used to be the
iterations alone, so a loop producing none was replaced by nothing and its
else went with it. That fixture is unroll_empty_for_else.txtar; this one is
what the fix must not disturb.

deny out/none/html/index.html `nothing here` -- the else body is the no-iteration case, so an unrolling that ran twice must not carry it

-- two.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    none {
        html
    }
}

const two list<int> = [1, 2]

component main node {
    vbox {
        for var x = two {
            text(value="item {x}")
        } else {
            text(value="nothing here")
        }
    }
}

window {
    main
}
-- out/none/html/index.html --
